---
// Tek Taraflı İşitme Kaybı — /ihtiyaciniza-gore/tek-tarafli-isitme-kaybi.
// Fifth page of the "İhtiyacınıza Göre" product-page series (see
// header.data.ts's devicesMega third column), following the completed
// four-page dB-degree ladder (Hafif/Orta/İleri/Çok İleri İşitme Kaybı).
// Built on the same master templates and shared, data-driven Brand
// Component Architecture, same KulakArkasiComparison component (already
// generic, reused as-is), same accent-scoping pattern with its own çinko
// grisi/zinc (#52525b) category accent — but this page covers a
// different classification axis entirely (laterality, not severity), so
// it does not extend the degree ladder.
//
// Deliberately scoped apart from the already-built Kablosuz Bağlantı
// Özellikleri page (/teknolojiler/kablosuz-baglanti), which already
// covers CROS/BiCROS as one of its four Ecosystem items: this page's own
// Ecosystem section cross-references that page's deep dive rather than
// re-explaining the same technology's internals, focusing instead on the
// symptoms, candidacy and CROS-vs-standard-fitting decision specific to
// single-sided loss.
//
// A health-classification topic, handled with the same care as the
// sibling degree pages and Tinnitus: self-diagnosis is never implied,
// and every section routes back to a proper audiometric evaluation
// (odyometri) — with this page's one real departure being that
// sudden-onset unilateral loss is flagged as needing urgent ENT (KBB)
// attention, not routine scheduling.
//
// 14-section flow, in order: Hero -> Nedir? + Nasıl Anlaşılır? ->
// Günlük Yaşamdaki Belirtiler -> Avantajları -> Dikkat Edilmesi
// Gerekenler -> Sistem Seçenekleri (CROS/BiCROS/standart/diğer) -> Öne
// Çıkan Özellikler -> Teknolojiler -> Önerilen Marka ve Modeller ->
// CROS/BiCROS vs Standart Tek Taraflı Amplifikasyon -> Uzman Yorumu ->
// SSS -> Premium CTA -> İlgili İçerikler.
// (BTE's "Kimler İçin Uygun" slot becomes everyday recognizable symptoms
// rather than candidacy, and BTE's hearing-loss-level slot becomes the
// real progression of solution approaches by how the better ear is
// affected — not a severity ladder, since this page's axis is laterality;
// see evolution.ts and ideal-user.ts.)
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import BrandPageHero from "../../components/brand-page/BrandPageHero/BrandPageHero.astro";
